## TIẾNG ANH · 16:30–17:00 — Thứ Ba: Giải thích khái niệm

### 16:30–16:40 · Shadowing

2 phút. Nghe → dừng → nhại to.

### 16:40–16:55 · Nói to có ghi âm

**Chủ đề: khi nào được dùng OTA, khi nào bắt buộc build lại.**

> *"Over-the-air updates let you ship JavaScript changes without going through the app stores. So bug fixes, copy changes, layout tweaks — all of that can go out in minutes instead of waiting days for review.*
> *The important limit is that OTA only replaces the JavaScript bundle. It cannot change native code. So if I install a library that has a native module, and I push that as an OTA update, the new JavaScript will call into native code that isn't there, and the app crashes on launch. And the user can't fix that themselves — you'd have to ship a store update.*
> *Expo handles this with runtime versions. An update is only delivered to builds with a matching runtime version. So when I change anything native, I bump the runtime version and do a real build.*
> *The rule I follow is simple: if the change touches package dot json in a way that adds native code, or touches app config like permissions or the icon, it needs a store build. Everything else can go OTA."*

### 16:55–17:00 · 5 từ mới

| Từ / cụm | Nghĩa | Câu mẫu |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `ship a fix` | phát hành bản sửa lỗi | *We shipped the fix in ten minutes.* |
| `bump` (v) | tăng số phiên bản | *I bump the runtime version.* |
| `call into` | gọi sang (tầng khác) | *JavaScript calls into native code.* |
| `on launch` | lúc khởi động app | *The app crashes on launch.* |
| `go through review` | qua khâu duyệt của store | *You don't have to go through review.* |

